,title,link,text,language,family
0,Music of Papua New Guinea - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Music_of_Papua_New_Guinea,"The music of Papua New Guinea encompasses a wide range of traditional and contemporary styles developed across the country's highly diverse ethnic groups. Traditional celebrations known as sing-sing feature communal song and dance, and form a central part of cultural life.",Isebe,Trans-New Guinea
1,Trans–New Guinea languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trans–New_Guinea_languages,"Trans–New Guinea is an extensive family of Papuan languages spoken on the island of New Guinea and neighboring islands, a region corresponding to the country Papua New Guinea as well as parts of Indonesia.",Isebe,Trans-New Guinea
2,Language: Isebe - transnewguinea.org,https://transnewguinea.org/language/isebe,"Classification: Nuclear Trans New Guinea, Madang, Croisilles, Mabuso, Gum, Panim-Isebe-Bau",Isebe,Trans-New Guinea
3,Papua New Guinea Traditional Songs (1 Hour Compilation ...Mamuna Tribe Songs (1 Hour Compilation) VOL. 2 - Tribal Music ...Music of Papua New Guinea - WikipediaTraditional Sounds of PNG - Paga Hill Estate - Port Moresby ...Music of Melanesia — GrokipediaThe Pamela J. Stewart and Andrew J. Strathern Archive,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Z05H4u8ZXNY,"Sep 19, 2025 · Papua New Guinea Traditional Songs (1 Hour Compilation) Tribal Music - Mamuna (Hypnotic) Perfect for: deep focus/work, mindful walking, meditation, breathwork, study, reading, nature... Oct 1, 2025 · Copyright Notice: All music and visuals featured on this channel are original creations by Tribal Echoes and are owned by the channel. The music of Papua New Guinea encompasses a wide range of traditional and contemporary styles developed across the country's highly diverse ethnic groups. Traditional celebrations known as sing-sing feature communal song and dance, and form a central part of cultural life. Jan 21, 2020 · Known as a place of ancient ritual and beauty, Papua New Guinea is also a nation of music, offering up its own unique soundtrack. From the sing-songs that occur at gatherings across the country to a variety of musical instruments used, here’s a snapshot of just some of the traditional sounds of PNG. The music of Melanesia encompasses the diverse traditional and contemporary musical practices of the indigenous peoples across the island chains of Papua New Guinea, the Solomon Islands, Vanuatu, Fiji, and New Caledonia, regions marked by over 1,100 languages and profound cultural variation. At ceremonial dances men and women play hour-glass drums and blow whistles in time with their dance movements and sung messages. At collective courting occasions, people sing songs and courting pairs turn their heads together expressively in time with the singing.",Isebe,Trans-New Guinea
